two independent node1<->node2 links and the private node3/node4 uplinks\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Sequential temporary-IP ping tests on all candidate interfaces cleanly identified node1 eth1<->node2 eth1, node1 eth2<->node2 eth2 as the two independent links, and node1 eth3<->node3, node2 eth3<->node4 as the private-network uplinks. All discovery IPs were removed after use.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-6a90118a63364f16\",\"cmd-ec99bead73a24a93\",\"cmd-2fb5f72dfc21495d\",\"cmd-4a17d216235c438b\",\"cmd-9716f492802d4c3c\",\"cmd-cca99a8563514ce7\",\"cmd-147af0287ecf4a4f\",\"cmd-35bd831ac3d9423d\"]},{\"id\":\"traffic-over-both-links\",\"requirement\":\"Carry traffic between the two private networks (node3/node4 subnets) over both independent links\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"ECMP static routes were installed on node1/node2 across both /31 point-to-point links (eth1 and eth2), each link was individually verified reachable, and node3->node4 traffic traversed the path successfully with per-interface counters on both eth1 and eth2 incrementing during a multi-ping test. The single-flow ping test showed asymmetric counter growth (fib_multipath_hash_policy=1 is L3-only, so a single src/dst ICMP flow is not expected to split across both links), so true concurrent load-spreading across a single flow was not directly demonstrated, but the ECMP configuration and per-link functional verification support the redundancy requirement as implemented.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-750fd84b73b242cf\",\"cmd-ee06d37e661c4ff3\",\"cmd-eda4edb481f24a3e\",\"cmd-a77fbf3de60c4284\",\"cmd-2b0233ad145e4c87\",\"cmd-cade90c98f454a2b\",\"cmd-eb2a1a16cded42dd\",\"cmd-1350cc962ab54121\",\"cmd-ac832db5b6c3400e\",\"cmd-a40c249365434018\",\"cmd-8989db92ee904a22\"]},{\"id\":\"failover-either-link\",\"requirement\":\"node3 and node4 keep reaching each other when either one of the two links is taken out of service\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Directly observed: baseline ECMP route on both node1 and node2, eth1 taken down on both nodes (kernel marked nexthop 'dead linkdown'), node3<->node4 ping succeeded with 0% loss via the surviving eth2 path, eth1 restored and route returned to full ECMP. The same bounded disruption/restoration cycle was then repeated symmetrically for eth2, with ping succeeding via the surviving eth1 path and full restoration confirmed afterward.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-9700c2a0ed0046a7\",\"cmd-b28c16f6b8864c16\",\"cmd-25a9f599bf574804\",\"cmd-c0869b6067934968\",\"cmd-da19042d00524b2b\",\"cmd-146f3d39be9c40d1\",\"cmd-2f4b7dd001814899\",\"cmd-ba78be5f5c77405d\",\"cmd-268f8eea1b724fb6\",\"cmd-70fe4deecbce4711\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node1\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol on node1: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service/data/cluster state\",\"status\":\"partially_satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id and reboot acknowledgement were captured, and the boot_id changed post-restart confirming an actual reboot. However, the automatic recovery mechanism (redundant-uplinks systemd oneshot service) did not restore the ECMP route on first boot (route absent immediately after restart), requiring the executor to manually re-run the apply script before full connectivity was confirmed. The design intended to be self-healing was not shown to work automatically in the observed restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-82a3333629544371\",\"cmd-04a14e0e8dec46f3\",\"cmd-394d60cfbc214bd0\",\"cmd-5248f7cec9804786\",\"cmd-086838aabc3f4bcd\",\"cmd-4a11aeeabade447e\",\"cmd-45e50c558d304c56\",\"cmd-af81b6c802cc4b46\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node2\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol on node2: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service/data/cluster state\",\"status\":\"partially_satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id and reboot acknowledgement were captured, and boot_id changed post-restart. The ECMP route was again missing after the automatic service ran (even with an initial retry-loop hardening applied before this reboot), requiring a manual re-run of the apply script to restore the route. A further-hardened script was written afterward but was never itself validated through an actual reboot of node2.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-73ebf37497c444db\",\"cmd-f16115910bce4e53\",\"cmd-074c7aa22e93450e\",\"cmd-8344af06ecea4768\",\"cmd-5ef310ba14384e7f\",\"cmd-c89bc56aa6e14216\",\"cmd-c85975d035214169\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node3\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol on node3: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service/data/cluster state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id captured, reboot acknowledged, post-restart boot_id changed, and NetworkManager's persisted static profile automatically restored the enp8s0 IP and route with no manual intervention; node3->node4 ping succeeded immediately after restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-388f8b9036eb4bd5\",\"cmd-e8c30e6743144f37\",\"cmd-f3d746d46c0941d3\",\"cmd-e4a210bf7ee14374\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node4\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol on node4: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service/data/cluster state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id captured, reboot acknowledged, post-restart boot_id changed, and NetworkManager's persisted static profile automatically restored the enp8s0 IP and route with no manual intervention; node4->node3 ping succeeded immediately after restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-138372374a65482c\",\"cmd-04599458df8947c3\",\"cmd-405aa9d5244940ed\",\"cmd-b6b0f2b0da3a4a39\"]}],\"confidence\":0.72,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.72,\"summary\":\"Executor performed an LACP bonding experiment on node1/node2 (creating bond0/br0, moving eth1/eth2/eth3 under them) that was ultimately abandoned due to a virtio mii_status limitation; this was a bounded